.TH BOOP 1 "" "Boop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
boop \- the Boop VPN app
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boop
[\fB\-\-autostart\fR] [\fB\-\-browser\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boop
opens the Boop window (WebKitGTK). It runs as the user and keeps its data in
\fI~/.config/boop\fR. The tunnel itself is held by
.BR boop-helper (8),
a system service; members of the group \fBboop\fR may use it.
Closing the window disconnects the VPN and quits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
start with the window minimised (used by \fI~/.config/autostart/boop.desktop\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-browser
open the window in the web browser instead (127.0.0.1, a random port and a
one-time link); also used by itself when no WebKitGTK window can be made.
.TP
.B \-\-version
print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/boop/
settings, the sign-in and \fIboop.log\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boop-helper (8)
